WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.527
A purchased list, a trade-show scan or a web form gives you prospects, not customers.

00:00:06.527 --> 00:00:10.597
This use case shows how to keep them apart as leads, call and

00:00:10.597 --> 00:00:14.788
text them, convert the ones that qualify, and follow the deals.

00:00:14.788 --> 00:00:19.100
It is a recap, and it points to the videos that show each screen.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:28.159
This is for managers and sales teams who work lists of prospects.

00:00:28.159 --> 00:00:34.690
Prospects live as leads, apart from your contacts, so your contact list holds only real customers.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:40.021
Agents and the dialer call and text leads exactly like contacts, and the

00:00:40.021 --> 00:00:44.250
outcome of each attempt moves the lead through your lead statuses.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.519
A lead that qualifies is converted.

00:00:47.519 --> 00:00:52.066
It becomes a contact, or merges into one who already has its number,

00:00:52.066 --> 00:00:56.060
joins an account, and can open an opportunity for the deal.

00:00:56.810 --> 00:01:02.930
Reports then show your lead funnel, which sources and lists convert best, and your pipeline.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:13.317
Your administrator turns on Omnichannel CRM, which also turns on Omnichannel Management, and

00:01:13.317 --> 00:01:16.599
Content Transfer to import lists, and Reports.

00:01:16.599 --> 00:01:20.450
The Omnichannel CRM starter recipe is the quickest way.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.921
Agents need Convert leads, and the Agent role has it.

00:01:24.921 --> 00:01:29.650
The manager needs Manage lead statuses and Manage opportunity stages.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.756
To call or text leads, you also need the features of an outbound

00:01:34.756 --> 00:01:37.120
calling campaign, or of texting.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:42.858
First, turn it on.

00:01:42.858 --> 00:01:48.306
The Omnichannel CRM starter recipe adds a Lead type that converts into Contact,

00:01:48.306 --> 00:01:52.600
a Sales Opportunity type, and a starting set of lead sources.

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:57.466
Second, review your lists under Interaction Center, Management:

00:01:57.466 --> 00:02:02.418
the lead statuses, which are open, closed or converted, the lead sources, and

00:02:02.418 --> 00:02:05.520
the opportunity stages with their probability.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:11.047
Third, import the list under Content, Import, with the lead type.

00:02:11.047 --> 00:02:15.285
Give the rows a list name, a lead source, a status and an

00:02:15.285 --> 00:02:20.600
owner, and skip numbers that already belong to a contact or an open lead.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:26.830
Fourth, open Leads to see your open leads, and search them by status,

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:29.460
source, list, rating or owner.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:38.178
Create an activity load with the lead type as the record type, and

00:02:38.178 --> 00:02:42.571
use the lead filters to pick, for example, one list's hot leads.

00:02:42.571 --> 00:02:47.278
A dialer load calls them, a manual load gives agents their lists, and

00:02:47.278 --> 00:02:50.290
an automatic load sends AI texts or calls.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:55.624
On the subject flow, set the lead status on each action, so that

00:02:55.624 --> 00:02:59.750
no answer moves the lead to Working, Contacted by itself.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:03.060
Open the lead and click Convert Lead.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:07.822
Pick or create the contact and the account, and tick Create an opportunity

00:03:07.822 --> 00:03:09.310
to record the deal.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:16.150
Track opportunities under Interaction Center, Opportunities, moving each one through its stages, and

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:19.540
see each company's contacts and deals under Accounts.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:25.408
Use the Lead funnel, Lead conversion by source and list, and Opportunity pipeline

00:03:25.408 --> 00:03:27.350
reports to see how it goes.

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:35.487
Import a small test list of two or three leads, with your own

00:03:35.487 --> 00:03:39.130
number on one of them, and find them by their list name.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:43.190
Convert one lead with Create an opportunity ticked.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:47.603
The lead leaves the Leads list and shows a Converted banner that links

00:03:47.603 --> 00:03:51.900
to the new contact, and the opportunity appears under Opportunities.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:55.109
Run the Lead funnel report for today.

00:03:55.109 --> 00:03:57.110
It counts the converted lead.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:04.689
A converted lead is read-only and never loaded again.

00:04:04.689 --> 00:04:08.984
Its history and open work move to the contact, and you cannot convert

00:04:08.984 --> 00:04:12.420
a lead while a call or message with it is in progress.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:17.707
When a number belongs to both a contact and a lead, inbound calls

00:04:17.707 --> 00:04:19.880
and texts match the contact.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:23.970
Keep Skip leads that are already contacts ticked on loads.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:28.899
To act when a lead converts, for example to send a welcome email,

00:04:28.899 --> 00:04:31.900
use a workflow that starts on Lead Converted.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:39.440
Leads kept apart, worked like contacts, converted when they qualify, and measured.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:46.113
Watch the videos on leads, on accounts and opportunities, and on loading activities for each screen.

00:04:46.113 --> 00:04:47.750
Thanks for watching.

